----------
scriptunit-fragment 1
----------

var b = 125

----------
scriptunit-fragment 2
----------

var w = 1

----------
scriptunit-fragment 3
----------

let e = b

----------
scriptunit-fragment 4
----------

let c = b + 1

----------
expect all four units are entered, the last after `b` is taken
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | compiles, runs | new | `b` moved |
| 2 | - | compiles, runs | new | `w` = 1 |
| 3 | takes `b` (1) | compiles, runs | new | `e` = 125 |
| 4 | - | compile fails | new, and `b` was taken | - |

----------
scriptunit-move 4 before 3
----------

----------
expect the reader moves above the take
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | reruns | rerun: unit 4 reads `b`, which unit 3 took after it | `b` moved |
| 2 | - | untouched | moving unit 4 changes nothing it reads | `w` = 1 |
| 4 | reads `b` (1) | recompiles, runs | moved | `c` = 126 |
| 3 | takes `b` (1) | reruns | takes `b` from unit 1 | `e` = 125 |

----------
scriptunit-move 2 after 4
----------

----------
expect a unit moves past units it has nothing to do with
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | untouched | nothing changed `b` | `b` moved |
| 4 | reads `b` (1) | untouched | nothing changed `b` | `c` = 126 |
| 2 | - | reruns | moved | `w` = 1 |
| 3 | takes `b` (1) | untouched | nothing changed `b` | `e` = 125 |
